 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Eight non-inverting buffers in two groups of four. Group 1 (1A1-1A4 to 1Y1-1Y4) is enabled by 1OE, group 2 (2A1-2A4 to 2Y1-2Y4) by 2OE. Both enables are active low."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output enable",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With its OE low, each Y output copies its A input. With OE high, the four outputs of that group go to high impedance whatever the A inputs do."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Input thresholds are TTL-compatible: VIH is 2 V min and VIL 0.8 V max over the whole 4.5 V to 5.5 V supply range. Input current is at most 1 µA. An input held at a TTL level rather than at a rail raises ICC by ΔICC, up to 2.9 mA per input (SN74HCT244)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Unused inputs",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "No input may be left floating; tie each unused one to VCC or GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output drive",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Outputs source and sink 6 mA at VCC = 4.5 V within the VOH and VOL limits, enough for 15 LSTTL loads, and suit bus lines and memory address drivers. Typical tpd is 13 ns at 5.5 V and 50 pF."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Quiescent ICC is at most 80 µA for the SN74HCT244 across its temperature range. Cpd is 40 pF per buffer, typical, at no load."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SN74HCT244 parts are rated -40 °C to 85 °C in PDIP (N), wide SOIC (DW), SOP (NS), SSOP (DB) and TSSOP (PW). SN54HCT244 parts are rated -55 °C to 125 °C in CDIP (J), CFP (W) and LCCC (FK), including SMD 5962-85130 and JM38510/65755 military versions. Catalog, automotive (SN74HCT244-Q1), enhanced (-EP), military and space (SN54HCT244-SP) versions exist."
  },
  {
   "topic": "SN74HCT244PWR",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SN74HCT244PWR is the SN74HCT244 in 20-pin TSSOP (PW), -40 °C to 85 °C, reel of 2000, marked HT244."
  }
 ],
